# Project memory

Canonical specs live in repo docs—this file is the **agent-facing distillate**. Patch this file **in-session** when triggers below fire; do not rely on chat memory alone.

## Self-update protocol

1. **Durable user preference** (style, tooling, process, things they want or never want again) → add or revise **User preferences** with `YYYY-MM-DD:` prefix.
2. **Deferred work** ("later", "not this PR", "backlog", agreed follow-up) → add **Parked / planned later** with what / why parked / optional trigger or link.
3. **Program fact changed** (new data source, new sequencing decision, merged milestone) → update **static sections** below and bump `last_reviewed` in frontmatter.
4. Keep bullets **short**; dedupe; retire superseded preference lines; move long narratives to `project.md`, `roadmap.md`, or `next_steps.md` instead of copying them here.

