## Long-term goals (north star)

- **Replayable history** at cutoffs—no post-`t` leakage.
- **Material forecasting:** strong baselines, calibration, evidence when graph beats tabular-at-same-cutoff.
- **Market-informed training** (Polymarket / Kalshi / peers) with masking—backbone must generalize beyond contract trivia.
- **Beyond listed contracts** at inference when scoped.
- **Learned query-conditioned subgraphs + assumptions** that earn their keep on held-out prediction and ablations—not baked historical priors dressed as discovery.
- **Interpretations tier:** ranked hypotheses + evidence + uncertainty; judged by HITL/rubrics—not fluency.
- **Constrained Q&A:** NL routes to retrieval + forecasts + cutoff; **LLM does not forecast alone.**

## Principles (roadmap P1–P7)

| ID | Principle |
|----|-----------|
| P1 | Forecastable ontology—two annotators can apply types to real evidence. |
| P2 | Temporal cleanliness—inputs only visible by `t`. |
| P3 | Baselines first—recurrence + tabular in comparable audits. |
| P4 | Graph earns complexity—ablations; retrieval/sparsity as ablatable as encoder/WM. |
| P5 | Markets supervise; they don't define the product—masking / non-market queries matter. |
| P6 | Discovery protocol—named regimes need post-hoc alignment/probes unless optional ablated covariates; assumptions inspectable. |
| P7 | Q&A constrained—LLM routes/summarizes; structured stack forecasts. |

## Strategic tie-breakers

- **Gradients before grand design:** thin correct loop on pinned snapshots → builder/subgraph + assumptions + minimal head → WM v0 → markets (`next_steps.md`).
- **Measurement over ontology:** minus-variants before new node types.
- **Parallel tracks:** builder supervision on **GDELT + ACLED** per contract; markets **Stage 3 for forecaster**, not builder; **WM after** pinned subgraph + assumptions; **France** = validation/smoke for builder, not primary training corpus; **Iran-like** lanes = shadow/red-team after WM + encoder ablation spine stable (`next_steps.md` §2.3).
- **Discovery vs naming:** statistical structure first; naming second with checks.

